#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096406 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "28008aa6-6be6-52dd-9459-097113538b13" :question/math-academy-id "e-501" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above expression through by $(x+2)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n2x-1= A(x-3)+B(x+2)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ term and allows us to solve for $A$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-2) - 1 &= A(-2 - 3) + B(-2 + 2) \\\\\n- 5 &= A(-5) + B(0) \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ term and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3) - 1 &= A(3 - 3) + B(3 + 2) \\\\\n5 &= A(0) + B(5) \\\\\nB &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$ and $B=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{1}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{1}{(x-3)}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096410 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "d10d11a8-6a30-59b6-bb0e-6065e60bbc6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-502" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} + \\dfrac{B}{x-3} + \\dfrac{C}{x+1}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ to clear the fractions:\n\n$$\n2x^2+5x+7= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+2)(x+1)+C(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $A$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-2)^{2} + 5(-2) + 7 &= A(-2 - 3)(-2 + 1) \\\\\n5 &= A(5) \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3)^{2} + 5(3) + 7 &= B(3 + 2)(3 + 1) \\\\\n40 &= B(20) \\\\\nB &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, plugging in $x=-1$ gets rid of the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-1)^{2} + 5(-1) + 7 &= C(-1 + 2)(-1 - 3) \\\\\n4 &= C(-4) \\\\\nC &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$, $B=2$, and $C=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{1}{x+2} +\\dfrac{2}{x-3} -\\dfrac{1}{x+1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b54bf81a-3d1f-54b2-97a2-2591a7cd0cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255554} {:answer/id #uuid "5b76a96e-e5a6-5d86-a602-3fdbdef26d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255555} {:answer/id #uuid "117ac078-4dba-5043-9edd-669649c5bf31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255556} {:answer/id #uuid "97481b2c-4c9d-57ff-8169-d95169d8f7fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255557} {:answer/id #uuid "da14403d-82b6-580c-a1ee-317936037b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "117ac078-4dba-5043-9edd-669649c5bf31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255556} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a76320-baf7-5e42-8f51-a960feca37c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255553}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d0e160a-5d6e-5ee6-93ac-1ec05397bce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-10940" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-2)x}=\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-2)x}=\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{x}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)x$ gives\n\n$$\nx-4=Ax+B(x-2).\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0-4 & =A(0)+B(0-2) \\\\ -4 & =-2B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-4 & =A(2)+B(2-2) \\\\ -2 & =2A \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{(x-2)x}=-\\frac{1}{(x-2)}+\\frac{2}{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA+B=-1+2=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c323c9-b4b7-55de-b8fb-b1fc59ed12ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255561} {:answer/id #uuid "3d30d3f4-7110-5d7a-94f1-05de257882c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255562} {:answer/id #uuid "db33c0c3-efd2-5101-8afc-0e00d60594ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255563} {:answer/id #uuid "3e25788b-7544-5f2b-9242-937076aff43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255564} {:answer/id #uuid "c348aa84-f04d-5685-8e7d-055cf33fe3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c323c9-b4b7-55de-b8fb-b1fc59ed12ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255561} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc4fc8d6-5aac-5a3d-a9b2-82befae980c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255560}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca8ed292-7934-54b0-b0fb-7d888622b0ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-10974" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(5-3x)(2x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n7x-37=A(2x+3)+B(5-3x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-\\frac{3}{2})-37 & =A(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+B(5-3(-\\frac{3}{2})) \\\\ \\frac{-21-74}{2} & =B(\\frac{10+9}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{-95}{2} & =B(\\frac{19}{2}) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-95}{19} \\\\ B & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{5}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(\\frac{5}{3})-37 & =A(2(\\frac{5}{3})+3)+B(5-3(\\frac{5}{3})) \\\\ \\frac{35-111}{3} & =A(\\frac{10+9}{3}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-76}{19} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90a7a256-59ae-55cd-8d2b-b5ebb7b49fc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255568} {:answer/id #uuid "8be77c94-126f-5205-8e6a-5871590a71aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255569} {:answer/id #uuid "72266f04-2ce9-5cc0-b94a-259d7536aca5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255570} {:answer/id #uuid "7990c164-2852-5090-b078-7a0559544676" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255571} {:answer/id #uuid "73783661-63f3-5253-94fd-8a09c1e7de0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72266f04-2ce9-5cc0-b94a-259d7536aca5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255570} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5e321b9-5af2-5635-9842-e9d3a66ea8da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255567}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "58617aa9-7162-5aab-b876-c11d9c41851e" :question/math-academy-id "q-10988" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{13{x}^{2}-19x-16}{(3x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A+B+C.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13{x}^{2}-19x-16}{(3x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n13{x}^{2}-19x-16=A(x-3)(x+1)+B(3x+2)(x+1)+C(3x+2)(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{2}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}-19(-\\frac{2}{3})-16 & =A(-\\frac{2}{3}-3)(-\\frac{2}{3}+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2)(-\\frac{2}{3}+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+1)(-\\frac{2}{3}-3) \\\\ \\frac{52}{9}+\\frac{38}{3}-16 & =A(\\frac{(-11)(1)}{9}) \\\\ \\frac{52+114-144}{9} & =A(-\\frac{11}{9}) \\\\ A & =-\\frac{22}{11} \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13(3)^{2}-19(3)-16 & =A(3-3)(3+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(3)+2)(3+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(3)+2)(3-3) \\\\ 117-57-16 & =B(44) \\\\ B & =\\frac{44}{44} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13(-1)^{2}-19(-1)-16 & =A(-1-3)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(-1)+2)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(-1)+2)(-1-3) \\\\ 13+19-16 & =C(4) \\\\ C & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+C & =(-2)+1+4=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eaec457-6db1-5d88-b4e1-668beca0dbda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eaec457-6db1-5d88-b4e1-668beca0dbda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd8ee49-ab79-5d64-b880-a2134d9614c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255574}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25acd6fd-eb49-59cd-9aef-224c06bf3730" :question/math-academy-id "q-350931" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{10}{(2x+1)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{10}{(2x+1)(x+3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2x+1$ |  | $x+3$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{(2x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{2x+1}-\\frac{2}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x+1)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n10=A(x+3)-2(2x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+3)-2(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\ 10 & =\\frac{5}{2}A \\\\ A & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{(2x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{4}{2x+1}-\\frac{2}{x+3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ff9dfce-adb7-537c-8233-3a021329fadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ff9dfce-adb7-537c-8233-3a021329fadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255578} :answer-field/id #uuid "c880ea29-f063-547c-b54f-94ece1dccf2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9d18b1d-0de4-5542-a385-ce43f89e72d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d18b1d-0de4-5542-a385-ce43f89e72d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255580} :answer-field/id #uuid "444b0666-38e4-597b-bb69-2acc4d8be561" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255579} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c4ea336-0017-5ee6-96ab-c98cd9a91713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c4ea336-0017-5ee6-96ab-c98cd9a91713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255582} :answer-field/id #uuid "909ea992-942a-534b-9425-8537e4e4468a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255581}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "44ef4936-3dea-54c1-850a-c1dc4cb391c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-351021" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{2{x}^{2}+11x+7}{(x-1)(x+3)(x+4)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{2{x}^{2}+11x+7}{(x-1)(x+3)(x+4)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $-$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-1$ |  | $x+3$ |  | $x+4$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}+11x+7}{(x-1)(x+3)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+3}+\\frac{C}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-1)(x+3)(x+4)$ gives\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+11x+7=A(x+3)(x+4)+B(x-1)(x+4)+C(x-1)(x+3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)^{2}+11(1)+7 & =A(1+3)(1+4)+B(1-1)(1+4)+C(1-1)(1+3) \\\\ 20 & =20A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-3)^{2}+11(-3)+7 & =A(-3+3)(-3+4)+B(-3-1)(-3+4)+C(-3-1)(-3+3) \\\\ -8 & =-4B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-4)^{2}+11(-4)+7 & =A(-4+3)(-4+4)+B(-4-1)(-4+4)+C(-4-1)(-4+3) \\\\ -5 & =5C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}+11x+7}{(x-1)(x+3)(x+4)}=\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{2}{x+3}-\\frac{1}{x+4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9569eac9-b380-56b7-afcc-094e36985865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255585} {:answer/id #uuid "0f4124b3-ba37-5bc6-87ef-d767239cdd8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255586} {:answer/id #uuid "f58ab48d-6efb-5194-8a0c-3fc07963b41c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 