\\\\  & \\,+B(4-4)(2(4)+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(4-4)(4+2) \\\\ 48+60 & =A(6)(9) \\\\ 108 & =54A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+15(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+2)(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-4)(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(-\\frac{1}{2}-4)(-\\frac{1}{2}+2) \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{15}{2} & =C(-\\frac{9}{2})(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ -\\frac{27}{4} & =-\\frac{27}{4}C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+C & =2+(-1)+1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
